WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.000
Who should replace Daniel Craig as James Bond?

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.100
One creative fan has a pretty good idea.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.380
Fan art depicting Henry Cavill as the superspy
has surfaced online, and it's good enough

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.750
that if Hollywood execs hadn't considered
casting Cavill in the role before, they're

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.300
probably mulling it over now.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.440
The image comes to us courtesy of digital
artist Jakub Maslowski via his Instagram account.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.020
It's stylish as all get-out, and that's because
Maslowski used his top-notch photo-editing

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:29.369
skills to alter a poster for the 2015 action-adventure
spy film The Man from U.N.C.L.E., in which

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:32.320
Cavill starred as the charming secret agent
Napoleon Solo.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.720
Maslowski was evidently inspired by a yet-unconfirmed
rumor that surfaced in September of last year

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.969
that claimed Cavill was being eyed to replace
Craig after next year's forthcoming as-yet

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:43.530
untitled Bond film.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.460
For that matter, Maslowski isn't the first
to have this idea.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.980
Fellow Photoshop wizard BossLogic also took
a crack at Cavill as Bond shortly before the

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.640
rumor started making the rounds.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.460
Both fan edits definitely have us hoping that
Cavill being up for the part is more than

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.320
just a rumor.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.300
The actor is, of course, best-known for portraying
Superman in recent DC movies.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:07.050
He held down the role in 2013's Man of Steel,
2016's Batman V. Superman: Dawn of Justice,

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.000
and 2017's Justice League.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.759
After that team-up film fell far short of
box office expectations, studio Warner Brothers

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.000
was forced to radically rethink its approach
to its DC properties.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.960
Rather than continue building a singular,
interconnected world like the Marvel Cinematic

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.220
Universe, Warner and DC went back to the drawing
board with a more filmmaker-driven approach

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.700
focusing more heavily on standalone films.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.200
So far, the results have paid dividends; this
year's Shazam!, which largely paid lip service

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.340
to the established continuity, scored with
critics and was a modest box office hit.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.180
Meanwhile, the upcoming Joaquin Phoenix starrer
Joker is already garnering early Oscar buzz.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:46.000
But as a result of the recalibration, characters
that were less warmly received by audiences,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.860
like Cavill's Superman, were sent back to
the drawing board.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:52.439
For Cavill, this means that he should have
some time on his hands, if he wants to jump

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.360
into yet another iconic franchise.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.720
Of course, it's not like the star is just
sitting around waiting for the phone to ring.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.540
He'll be holding down the lead role of Geralt
in Netflix's upcoming, highly-anticipated

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.580
live-action adaptation of The Witcher.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:07.720
He's also attached to star as Sherlock Holmes
in Enola Holmes, which will see Stranger Things'

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.080
Millie Bobby Brown appearing as the titular
younger sister of the legendary detective.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.140
But few actors would sneeze at the opportunity
to play 007, and if the stars line up right,

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:22.510
the 36-year old Englishman could potentially
hold down the role of 007 for years to come,

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.620
just as Daniel Craig has.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:28.319
The blond Brit has made a fine Bond, admirably
filling the superspy's shoes in four films

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.840
before agreeing to come back for one more
round in the physically taxing role.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.540
The upcoming Bond movie has had its share
of bumps in the road on the way to screens,

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:40.640
but sneak peaks released by director Cary
Joji Fukunaga promise a rollicking, globetrotting

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.720
sendoff for Craig.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.760
It's doubtful that we'll get any official
Bond casting news until after the final Daniel

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.640
Craig Bond flick is released on April 8, 2020,
but until then, this image should help to

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.600
give fans, executives, and casting directors
some serious food for thought.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.640
Cavill is a gifted actor, he certainly looks
the part, and he's British to boot.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.629
Thank you, Mr. Maslowski, for creatively stating
the obvious, this man needs to be the next

00:03:03.629 --> 00:03:04.320
007.

